# 3.3.1.blueprint.product — enroll with interface

> the implementation blueprint the execution will adhere to. grounded in the criteria
> ([`2.1`](./2.1.criteria.blackbox.yield.md), [`2.2`](./2.2.criteria.blackbox.matrix.yield.md)) and the
> research ([`3.1.1`](./3.1.1.research.external.product.flagged._.yield.md),
> [`3.1.3.prod`](./3.1.3.research.internal.product.code.prod._.yield.md),
> [`3.1.3.test`](./3.1.3.research.internal.product.code.test._.yield.md)). follows the repo's extant
> patterns: `(input, context)`, arrow-only, get/set/gen verbs, inline i/o contracts, directional deps,
> one-op-per-file, BDD tests, blackbox acceptance via the self-linked `bin/run`.

---

## summary

deliver the **actor/clone frame** + the **talk** surface (`list` / `say` / `get`), in scope per the
wisher's answers. concretely:

1. **enroll routes through a managed pty.** the extant direct `spawn(..., { stdio: 'inherit' })` becomes
   a **managed-pty spawn** that (a) mirrors the brain to the human's terminal invisibly, and (b) stands
   up a per-clone **unix domain socket** for dispatch. a **plain-spawn fallback** covers an absent pty
   addon, a non-capable brain, or a headless `-p` run.
2. **every enroll leaves a durable record** under `.agent/.actors/actor.via.hash=$hash/` — an
   **anonymous** actor (hash namespace only; enroll never consults `actors.yml`), which holds the shared
   brain config, an append-only roles log, and a `clones/` dir. each run is a **clone** with a `serial`,
   an optional `--as @:<slug>` handle, an `identity.json`, a `socket`, and a `history/` of symlinks to
   the brain-cli's own transcripts.
3. **the talk verbs reach a clone** with no keyboard: `rhx actor list`, `rhx clone list [@<actor>]`,
   `rhx clone say @:<slug|serial> --what <m>`, `rhx clone get @:<slug|serial> [--tail N]`. all four
   carry a **`--output tree|json`** flag (default `tree`): `tree` is the human treestruct, `json` emits
   the already-computed structured domain result as machine-parseable JSON (i007-r12-2) — because the
   wish's WHOLE motive is machine consumption ("ipc programatic access of clones… crons, comms"), and a
   cron/webhook parsing box-drawing glyphs is fragile. this mirrors the extant `git.commit.push
   --output json` compose-seam: the `json` branch is a thin `JSON.stringify` of the domain result the
   `tree` branch already renders (no new domain op), so the two outputs never drift. the tree-vs-json
   SELECTION is a ONE shared `renderCliOutput` op (i010-r11-B) the four invokers compose, not a branch
   re-implemented 4× — so it cannot drift as the talk surface grows.
4. **the brain input widens** to three forms — absent (→ default brain), `--brain <b>`, positional
   `<b>` — with a fail-loud on conflict.
5. **config application (init/link) reaches every actor dir**, not the repo root alone.

**bake** (`make`/`fork`/`wake`) and the `actors.yml` slug namespace are **out of scope** (the `rhx clone`
dream). the socket is proven end-to-end by TWO tiers, never a mock (i022-r09-1/2): (a) a HERMETIC
**stub-brain acceptance test** — the fast, credential-free CI gate that proves the socket mechanism
deterministically (enroll → say → get, no network, no cost); AND (b) a **real-claude external-contract
acceptance test** — the genuine external AI service call, credential-gated + FAIL-LOUD when the
credential is absent (the SAME pattern the repo's other external-contract integration tests use, e.g.
declastruct-stripe's `getStripeCredentials()` fail-loud), NEVER a playtest deferral. per
rule.require.external-contract-integration-tests + the behaver verification philosophy ("mocks lie;
credential difficulty is a blocker, not a deferral"), the stub proves the mechanism but the REAL claude
proves the integration, so BOTH are required deliverables — the stub is not a substitute for the real
call, it is the fast complement to it.

### the pivotal decisions (fulcrums — best-guessed, flagged for the end-of-road council)

| # | fulcrum | best guess | clean rework? |
|---|---------|-----------|---------------|
| F1 | pty lib | **`node-pty`**, loaded **lazily** on the node/tsx (jit) branch enroll already runs on — so the bun/JSC `.node`/V8 incompatibility (per [3.1.1 topic-5, src 34]; reconciled by [src 33,35,36] N-API prebuilds) never applies, per the OPIN in [3.1.1 topic-5]; a `bun-pty` swap ([3.1.1 topic-5, src 37,38]) stays behind one adapter file | yes — one communicator file `genBrainCliPtyClone.ts` |
| F2 | socket location | `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/clone.$serial.$homeHash.sock` — **mirrors the extant `getKeyrackDaemonSocketPath` convention** (host-scoped, tmpfs, 0700, short enough to dodge the ~104-char unix-socket path limit a repo-nested `.agent/.actors/.../socket` would blow). the clone DIR keeps identity+history; the socket lives in runtime | yes — one path transformer (`getCloneSocketPath`) |
| F3 | dispatch frames | `say` wraps the message in **bracketed-paste** markers + a submit `\r` (per [3.1.1 topic-3, src 17] Ink bracketed-paste; injection precedent [src 20,21,24]) | yes — one transformer `asCloneDispatchFrame` |
| F4 | liveness | **derived** from socket connectability, never a stored state field ([1.vision cons]) | yes — `isCloneLive` is the only reader |
| F5 | actor on-disk identity object | **reuse** `BrainCliEnrollmentManifest` + `genEnrollmentHash` ([3.1.3.prod src 7]) as the actor identity, wrapped in a thin persisted **`ActorEnrolled`** entity (hash-keyed) so `Clone.actor` has a real referent; add **two** domain objects — `ActorEnrolled` (on-disk enrolled identity) + `Clone` — as peers of the extant in-memory `Actor` ([3.1.3.prod src 10,11]). the extant `Actor` (live `act`/`run`/`ask`, keyed `role.slug`) is a DIFFERENT grain, not the on-disk record — so it is NOT reused as the persisted actor (blocker-2 fix: the earlier "add only a `Clone`" undercounted by one object) | yes — additive |
| F6 | ActorEnrolled object kind | **DomainEntity** (primary≡unique=hash) — kept over the honester **DomainLiteral** (content-addressed value) for ONE reason: `Clone.actor` needs a typed `RefByPrimary<ActorEnrolled>` (blocker-2), and key-based Ref is an entity concept. the reviewer is right the Entity-with-primary≡unique is a content-addressed value in an identity shape (i005-nitpick-6). CONCRETE HAZARD (i009-r11-3): DomainEntity is the `.clone({…})`-mutation idiom, so a future `.clone({brain:…})` could mint a hash-mismatched record — the exact bug the "immutable by construction" prose forbids. RESOLUTION (b) taken NOW so the invariant is verified not just declared: ActorEnrolled.test.ts asserts hash===genEnrollmentHash({brain,roles}) for the record's own fields (a mismatched record is caught); if the council picks DomainLiteral (option a), the same guard holds | yes — one object + one Clone field: DomainLiteral + a hash-typed ref (the guard test carries either way) |

