│   │   │   ├── isCloneSocketEligible.ts                  [+] transformer (nitpick-4 i004; input widened i042-r11-5) — `{ brain, interactive, noSocket, outputIsJson } → boolean`: isBrainSocketCapable(brain) AND (interactive OR outputIsJson) AND NOT noSocket. the socket-path gate as a NAMED pure transformer, NOT inline decode-friction in genClone (rule.forbid.decode-friction-in-orchestrators). the `interactive OR outputIsJson` DISJUNCTION lives INSIDE this pure op (i042-r11-5 fix — it was an unnamed OR at invokeEnroll's call site: `--output json` opts a non-TTY machine spawn into eligibility "in lieu of isInteractiveTty", so the real gate input is `isInteractiveTty() OR outputIsJson` — the ONE branch left ad-hoc while every comparable one (computeBrainCliInput, computeCloneSlugDecision) was extracted). folding `outputIsJson` into this op's input names + unit-tests the disjunction (a headless `--output json` spawn IS eligible; a headless non-json spawn is NOT), so the machine-handoff eligibility rule has one tested owner, not a call-site OR
│   │   │   ├── isInteractiveTty.ts                       [+] communicator (nitpick-4 i004) — `process.stdout.isTTY` → boolean; NAMES where `interactive` comes from (a headless `-p` one-shot → false → fallback, no socket)
│   │   │   └── getPtyModuleOrNull.ts                     [+] communicator (i011-r12-C1 — the pty-addon-load GATE, a mechanism DISTINCT from --no-socket): LAZY-require `node-pty` inside a try/catch that ALLOWLISTS ONLY the module-load error (MODULE_NOT_FOUND / a native-ABI load throw — a load failure of the OPTIONAL native addon, per package.json's optionalDependency), returns the loaded module OR null; any OTHER error re-throws (rule.forbid.failhide — never swallow a real fault). this is the RUNTIME half of the fallback the vision names ("pty native module absent / fails to load → fall back to plain stdio:'inherit' spawn with a loud one-line notice"), which isCloneSocketEligible (a PURE transformer over {brain,interactive,noSocket}) structurally CANNOT cover — a clone can be socket-ELIGIBLE by brain+interactive+not-noSocket yet the addon still fails to load on THIS host. so the two triggers are SEPARATE by design: --no-socket / headless / brain-incapable → isCloneSocketEligible=false (an EXPECTED, quiet fallback); addon-load-failure → this gate returns null (the LOUD one-line notice, because the human asked for a socket + capability said yes, but the native addon broke). genClone composes BOTH: the pty path runs only if isCloneSocketEligible AND getPtyModuleOrNull() !== null; a load-failure records socketEligible=false + emits the notice. SPAWN-TIME ALLOCATION FAILURE — A DISTINCT, THIRD FALLBACK TRIGGER (i050-r12-new fix — the sandbox hazard the fresh holistic pass named): a SUCCESSFUL `require('node-pty')` does NOT guarantee `pty.spawn()` SUCCEEDS at CALL time — allocating a pty needs `/dev/ptmx`, which is UNAVAILABLE or permission-denied in a sandboxed container without a pty mount (Docker without pty passthrough, some CI runners, restricted agentic sandboxes). this is DIRECTLY in this tool's operating context: it spawns brain-CLIs (claude-code) that FREQUENTLY run INSIDE exactly such a sandbox, so a spawn-time EACCES/ENOENT on the pty device is a COMMON host, not a rare one — and an un-wrapped spawn would HARD-FAIL enroll on it, breaking the vision's "never hard-fail from install THROUGH runtime" promise (the module-load gate covers install/load, this covers the untested runtime-allocation half). so genBrainCliPtyClone's actual `pty.spawn()` call is wrapped with the SAME allowlist-and-fallback discipline as getPtyModuleOrNull's load: a spawn-time EACCES/ENOENT/ENXIO on the pty device is ALLOWLISTED → genBrainCliPtyClone returns a null-spawn signal → genClone FALLS BACK to enrollBrainCli plain-spawn + the SAME loud one-line notice (socketEligible=false), exactly as the addon-load-failure path; any OTHER spawn error re-throws (rule.forbid.failhide — only the pty-device-allocation faults are allowlisted). so the fallback ladder now has THREE runtime triggers, each named + distinct: (1) --no-socket / headless / brain-incapable → quiet expected fallback (isCloneSocketEligible=false); (2) addon fails to LOAD → loud notice (getPtyModuleOrNull null); (3) addon loads but pty ALLOCATION fails at spawn → loud notice (the spawn-time allowlist). a genBrainCliPtyClone.integration row forces a spawn-time EACCES (a mocked pty.spawn that throws the device error) → asserts the fallback + notice, and any non-device spawn error re-throws — the SAME shape as getPtyModuleOrNull's load-failure test
