carries `infra/`/`sdk/`/`svc/` subtrees with `index.ts` barrel entrypoints (the internal-organization
shape), BUT it has **NO `package.json` and NO `_topublish/` anywhere under `keyrack/daemon`** (confirmed:
glob of `keyrack/daemon/**/package.json` + `keyrack/daemon/**/_topublish*/**` → no matches; the only
non-subtree file is `daemon.integration.test.ts`). so it is an **in-app module**, NOT an independently
published package — the infra/sdk/svc folders are internal organization, not an extraction boundary. THEREFORE
the lift to the main-app `src/infra/` is CORRECT (it breaks no standalone-publish boundary, and honors
`rule.require.directional-deps` — both the clone domain and the keyrack daemon are in-app consumers of one
shared `src/infra/`). the conditional is closed: lift to `src/infra/`, no neutral-package indirection needed.
