│   ├── cloneEnvKeys.ts                                   [+] const (i042-r11-4 fix + i043-r11-1 LAYER fix — the undeclared-magic-string gap, now homed in the cross-layer utils/ tier NOT domain.operations/clone/): the ONE named home for the self-identification env-var KEYS — `export const CLONE_ENV = { serial: 'RHACHET_CLONE_SERIAL', socket: 'RHACHET_CLONE_SOCKET' } as const`. WHY the keys need one home: WRITTEN by genBrainCliPtyClone (clone/pty/) AND enrollBrainCli (infra/enroll/), READ by invokeCloneWhoami (contract/cli/) — three sites in three folders; as a bare literal at each, a rename/typo in ONE writer silently breaks `whoami` for only that spawn path (a compiler-invisible drift), as ONE imported const a rename is a single edit + a type error at any stale reader (rule.require.ubiqlang: one canonical name; the SAME single-source discipline getSupportedBrainCommand's `.socket` field carries). WHY utils/ NOT domain.operations/clone/ (i043-r11-1 blocker fix — the directional-deps cycle): a home under `domain.operations/clone/` would force `infra/enroll/enrollBrainCli.ts` to import UPWARD (infra → domain.operations), and since `domain.operations/clone/genClone.ts` already imports enrollBrainCli DOWNWARD (domain.operations → infra, the sanctioned direction), the pair closes a real folder-level cycle `genClone → enrollBrainCli → cloneEnvKeys` — a rule.require.directional-deps violation (infra must "depend on none") baked straight into the filediff tree, the exact defect-class an executor would ship if it followed the tree literally. a zero-dependency `export const` is the textbook `utils/` case (the repo's own rule: utils/ is cross-layer, available to all, depends on none), so all THREE consumers import it with NO directional violation and NO cycle — one file's path line moves, three import paths update, no other cascade. this is the correctly-tiered twin of getSupportedBrainCommand's shared-registry read (which stays in infra/enroll/ because its consumers sit DOWNWARD in domain.operations/clone/pty/; cloneEnvKeys' consumers straddle infra AND contract AND domain.operations, so only the cross-layer utils/ tier serves all three without a cycle). NO dedicated `cloneEnvKeys.test.ts` — DELIBERATE, not a coverage gap (i044-r11-2): it is a bare `export const {…} as const` with no logic to unit-test, so per rule.prefer.wet-over-dry a trivial const earns no test; a stale key is a TYPE ERROR at every importer (the single-source guarantee that motivated the const), and the three consumers' own tests (enrollBrainCli + genBrainCliPtyClone env-injection readback, invokeCloneWhoami env read) exercise the values end-to-end
│   ├── cloneDispatchFrame.ts                             [+] const (i045-r11-1/r12-1 fix — the SHARED dispatch-frame wire-protocol sentinel, the EXACT cloneEnvKeys defect-class applied to the frame protocol): the ONE named home for the bracketed-paste frame markers + submit byte the dispatch wire protocol agrees on — `export const CLONE_DISPATCH_FRAME = { pasteStart: '\e[200~', pasteEnd: '\e[201~', submit: '\r' } as const`. WHY it needs one home: THREE ops in the same clone/socket/ folder independently reference "the bracketed-paste sentinel" today — asCloneDispatchFrame (WRITES pasteStart + body + pasteEnd + submit, the client frame), asCloneDispatchFrameSplit (WATCHES for pasteEnd + submit to REASSEMBLE the byte-stream into whole frames), and isSafeCloneDispatchInput (REJECTS an embedded pasteEnd mid-body, the frame-forgery guard) — a THREE-site-agreement requirement with a DUAL ROLE that makes silent drift WORSE than cloneEnvKeys': pasteEnd is a boundary MARKER on the write+reassemble paths AND FORBIDDEN CONTENT on the guard path, so a future edit that tightens/loosens the terminator bytes in ONE file desyncs reassembly or the forgery-guard with NO compiler error (a frame silently split wrong, or a forged frame silently admitted). this is the SAME multi-site-literal-drift defect cloneEnvKeys fixed for CLONE_ENV (i042/i043) and getSupportedBrainCommand's `.socket` field fixed for the brain registry — the review history's own recurring blind spot ("a newly-added surface reintroduces a bug-class already fixed elsewhere"), closed here by the SAME single-const discipline: all three ops IMPORT `CLONE_DISPATCH_FRAME`, so the frame format has ONE owner and a terminator change is a single edit with no stray literal left to drift. LAYER = utils/ NOT clone/socket/ for the SAME future-proofing cloneEnvKeys carries: the three consumers are all in clone/socket/ today (so a clone/socket/ home would NOT cycle right now), BUT the dream's `wake`/`fork` reach for the frame from clone/pty/ + a potential contract-layer relay, which would straddle layers exactly as cloneEnvKeys' consumers do — so utils/ is the tier that keeps the two frame-protocol consts SYMMETRIC in one cross-layer place and avoids a later relocation. NO dedicated `cloneDispatchFrame.test.ts` — DELIBERATE (same as cloneEnvKeys, i044-r11-2): a bare `export const {…} as const` with no logic; a stale marker is a TYPE ERROR at every importer, and the three consumers' own tests (asCloneDispatchFrame frame-shape, asCloneDispatchFrameSplit reassembly, isSafeCloneDispatchInput forgery-reject) exercise the values end-to-end
