## codepath tree

> legend: `[+]` create · `[~]` update · `[○]` retain · `[-]` delete · `[←]` reuse · `[→]` eject

```
rhx enroll [brain] [--brain b] [--roles spec] [--as @:slug] [--no-socket]  [~] invokeEnroll
├── computeBrainCliInput({ positional, flag, default })                  [+] transformer — 3-form derive, fail-loud on conflict
│   └── genActor default-brain rule (brains[0])                       [←] reuse [3.1.3.prod:12]
├── getBrainCliPassthroughArgs({ rawArgs, brain, asSlug, socketOff })  [~] EXTEND getRawArgsAfterEnroll [3.1.3.prod:1] — strip EVERY enroll-consumed token from the passthrough: the resolved brain in all 3 forms (positional token by value, OR the `--brain <b>` PAIR), plus the NEW `--as @:<slug>` pair and the `--no-socket` flag — so none of enroll's own flags leak into the spawned brain's argv (absent brain → strip no brain token)
├── parseBrainCliEnrollmentSpec / getRoleDeltaTokens                  [←] reuse [3.1.3.prod:4]
├── computeBrainCliEnrollment({ brain, spec, rolesDefault })          [○] retain
├── genEnrollmentHash({ enrollment })                                 [←] reuse [3.1.3.prod:7] → the actor identity
├── getOneRepoPath({ cwd: process.cwd() })                            [+] communicator (i040-r11-B1) — the ONE canonical-repoPath derivation, at the cli boundary; `fs.realpathSync(cwd)` follows symlinks + strips the trailing slash so two equivalent cwds converge to ONE `repoPath`. its output is THREADED into findsertActorEnrolled + genClone below (and, in the talk verbs, into getOneCloneByRef / getAllClonesGroupedByActor / getOneActorEnrolledByRef) — NEVER a raw process.cwd() at a consuming op, so the composite {repoPath, hash} identity can never fragment across a symlinked/worktree/macOS-alias path
├── findsertActorEnrolled({ enrollment, repoPath })                     [+] orchestrator — repoPath is the getOneRepoPath-canonical value (never raw cwd)
│   ├── getActorEnrolledDir({ repoPath, hash })                               [+] transformer
