└── getAllActorsEnrolled({ repoPath })                                  [+] communicator → treestruct stdout (reuse the extant getSkillListTreestruct render pattern [←], NOT a new tree renderer). ABBREVIATED HASH DEFAULT (i013-r12-C fix — complete the git analogy): the TREE render abbreviates each actor hash to a git-style SHORT PREFIX (12 chars, e.g. `9c1e4d2a8b3f`), NOT the raw 64-char sha256 — because the blueprint borrows git's prefix-match reach (`@<hash-prefix>`, uc11), and git's other half is `--oneline`'s abbreviated DISPLAY; a 64-char hash per line is the visual-blemish the analogy exists to avoid. 12 chars keeps collisions astronomically unlikely at any realistic actor count while staying copy-pasteable as a prefix. the FULL hash is always reachable via `--output json` (the machine wants the whole key), so no information is lost — the human sees a short handle, the machine gets the full one. same tree-abbreviates / json-emits-full split as the since=/spawnedAt field

