tity.json carrying the dream's future REQUIRED-in-v2 `lastActivityAt` field with `schemaVersion:1` (a v1 record that a v2 build will later add the field to) → this v1 build reads it clean (extra field tolerated), AND seed a `schemaVersion:2` record on this v1 build → fail-loud upgrade hint; a reorder to a strict-exact-shape check → the extra-field record reads corrupt + `clone list` hard-crashes on every extant clone + the assertion goes red (proving the tolerance closes the self-inflicted local-upgrade break the review named)
