o at every instant `clone list` shows EXACTLY the winner (one published serial) or no row, DETERMINISTIC across repeated runs. DOGFOODED: force the loser to pause AFTER its temp-dir bake but BEFORE its reap, then a concurrent `clone list` → the loser's temp dir is NOT in the result (the `serial=*` filter excludes it), so the ghost row the r7 blocker named can never appear; a reorder that renames-before-claim → the ghost row reappears + the assertion goes red (which proves the claim-before-rename order is essential, not incidental). + LOSER-ORPHAN-BRAIN (i033-r07-1, the fresh r7 fix — the reap now KILLS its pty child): the concurrent-bake loser terminates its brain process BEFORE it removes its temp dir — asserted the loser's pty child is DEAD after the reap, so no orphan brain draws credits with no clone record left to detect it. DOGFOODED: two concurrent same-actor `--as @:driver` bakes, capture the loser's pty child pid, then after the reap assert `process.kill(pid, 0)` throws ESRCH (the child is gone); a reorder that removes the temp dir WITHOUT the pty.kill() → the child stays alive + the assertion goes red (which proves the kill-child step is essential to the reap sequence, not incidental)
