├── invokeCloneList.integration.test.ts                    [+] integration — `clone list` unscoped GROUPS clones under each actor header across MULTIPLE actors (brain+roles ON the actor header, blocker-6; not a flat dump); tri-state per clone line — LIVE / DEAD / NOT-REACHABLE (blocker-5); scoped `@<actor>` resolves an ANONYMOUS hash-actor ref via the hash literal (blocker-4) → only that actor's clones; unknown scope ref → fail-loud; `--output json` → machine-parseable array carrying serial/slug/reach-state/brain/roles + the RAW `spawnedAt` IsoTimeStamp (i012-r12-4: NOT a rendered "since=2m ago" string — a machine reads the absolute instant; the relative `since=<ago>` is the tree-only render) + the structured `orphan` field (i039-r11-5/r12-1): a suspected-orphan DEAD clone → `orphan: { suspectedPid: <n> }` in its json entry, a live / cleanly-dead / cross-host / recycled-pid clone → `orphan: null` — asserted a CRON reads `entry.orphan?.suspectedPid` as a FIELD (never a regex over the tree suffix), and that the SAME clone's tree render carries the `(orphan? pid <n> …)` advisory iff its json `orphan` is non-null (ONE isCloneOrphanProcess computation, both renders, can't disagree); unknown `--output` value → fail-loud
