I session's cost + latency + occasional service flakiness do NOT tax every PR yet the genuine integration is proven before each release. the credential-gated fail-loud still holds AT the release gate (a release without the claude credential fails loud, never ships green-by-skip), so the real integration is a hard release precondition — bounded cadence, not absent coverage. PER-RUN COST/TIME CEILING (i046-r11-nit — the cadence policy bounds WHEN it runs, not how much ONE run costs if the real session hangs): the test wraps its real say→get round-trip in a HARD per-run timeout (a bounded IsoDuration budget, generous for a real reply but finite) — a real claude session that hangs or waits on an unexpected TUI state ABORTS at the ceiling + FAILS-LOUD MalfunctionError that names the timeout, rather than run unbounded on the release gate's clock/credits. so a single misbehaved run has a capped cost, which complements the cadence policy that caps run FREQUENCY — together they bound both how often AND how expensively the external call can run

