## i062 fold addendum (post-condense L3 round)

> the body ABOVE is the frozen i059-era verbatim record. this addendum records the folds landed AFTER the
> `.md`/`.md.full` condense split, so the two files never disagree — the distillate `.md` carries these same
> decisions inline; here is their provenance.

### r11 (enroll-blueprint-arch-defects, L3) — 2 blockers + 2 nitpicks, ALL folded at source

- **blocker r11-1 — the ambiguous-refuse guard never converges (a starved-forever `history/`).** the i059
  fold made `genCloneHistoryLink` REFUSE to link on 2+ unclaimed candidates in the spawn window
  (`transcriptMtime >= spawnedAt`), which closes the cross-actor content-bleed — but a refused candidate was
  never excluded from the "unclaimed" pool, and the window only grows, so two co-located clones (the
  `-driver`/`-foreman` one-cwd inventory case) refuse FOREVER → a permanently empty `history/`, not just for
  that one episode. **fold:** on refusal, write an atomic `.exids/<exid>.ambiguous` quarantine claim per
  refused candidate (the same `genAtomicSymlinkClaim` primitive `.slugs/`/`.exids/` use). a quarantined exid
  leaves the eligible pool, so the pool only shrinks — convergence restored, no permanent-empty history for
  the mandated worktree crew.
- **blocker r11-2 — the `exidsAmbiguous` WARN was dead code (no cross-process persistence).** the refusal
  happens inside the `rhx enroll` process; `rhx clone get` is a SEPARATE later process that reads only what is
  symlinked in `history/`; a refused exid was never symlinked, so `getCloneOutput` could only ever return
  `exidsAmbiguous: []` and the promised "never a silent empty" WARN never fired. **fold:** the quarantine
  marker from r11-1 IS the durable cross-process path — `getCloneOutput` populates `exidsAmbiguous` by a small
  filtered read of the `.exids/*.ambiguous` markers (kept for exids whose transcript passes
  `isTranscriptWithinSpawnWindow` against THIS clone's `spawnedAt`), never a re-run of the linker's discovery
  (the decompose-for-recompose violation i061 flagged). the WARN now fires; an acceptance snapshot
  (`clone.samecwd-race.acceptance`) clamps the user-visible empty+WARN, the clamp the i059 mechanism-level
  test lacked.
- **the shared root + the pre-flagged lift.** both blockers share one root, closed by one addition. the
  inline mtime+spawn-window heuristic lifts to a pure `isTranscriptWithinSpawnWindow({transcriptMtime,
  spawnedAt}) → boolean` — the i010-r11-D ledger PRE-FLAGGED this lift to fire on its second consumer, and
  `getCloneOutput`'s quarantine read IS that second consumer, so the pre-declared trigger fires now (one pure
  owner of the window rule, shared by the linker + the observe path).
- **nitpick r11-nit-1 — `reachState` wiring.** `computeCloneUnreachableHint` returns `{message,hint}`, so
  `asCliErrorJson`'s `reachState` projection had no source. **fold:** the reach invoker (say/get) attaches the
  `getCloneReachState` value onto the ConstraintError metadata; `asCliErrorJson` reads that field.
- **nitpick r11-nit-2 — clone-env-injection wet with no tripwire.** the `RHACHET_CLONE_SERIAL`/`_SOCKET`
  injection is wet across `enrollBrainCli` + `genBrainCliPtyClone` (two spawn branches). **fold:** a
  rule-of-three tripwire — the dream's `wake` = the 3rd branch → extraction to a shared
  `genCloneChildEnv({serial, socketPath})` off `cloneEnvKeys`.
- **nitpick r11-nit-4 — `clone/` flat file count crossed the "3+ earns a subfolder" trigger.** **HELD** as a
  reactive filesystem reshuffle at execution: a pure directory move with zero design/dependency change (a
  nitpick, self-stated), and the two clusters that carry a real cross-folder edge (`clone/pty/` +
  `clone/socket/`) are already nested; the flat leaves have no such edge, so a distillate reshuffle now buys
  churn without a design gain.

### r12 (enroll-blueprint-behavior-intent, L3) — 0 blockers + 4 nitpicks, all already-tracked

r12 found NO new blockers and confirmed no divergence from wish/vision intent. its four nitpicks are each an
already-ledgered deferral, re-surfaced at the acceptance-coverage angle:

- **r12-nit-1 — say-vs-a-human's-own-live-keystrokes has no journey-level acceptance test.** HELD — the same
  hazard as ledger row 2(i054): the human's raw stdin is a DIRECT `stdin→pty.write` passthrough by the uc1
  invisible-mirror mandate, so a per-line interlock fights a uc1 hard requirement; the garble is bounded +
  visible (bracketed-paste), and the stricter interlock is a council + playtest fulcrum. the CURRENT render
  gets a snapshot-clamp at execution so a further regression is caught.
- **r12-nit-2 — the cross-actor-same-cwd `get` degradation had no end-to-end snapshot.** this is the
  user-experience symptom of r11-2, and the r11-2 fold's `clone.samecwd-race.acceptance` snapshot closes it
  directly.
- **r12-nit-3 — `since=spawnedAt` does not deliver the vision's "idle 20m" and no snapshot pins the current
  render.** HELD — the same wisher-visible scope-cut as the `since=<spawn>` ledger row (idle needs a
  per-dispatch `lastActivityAt` → the dream); the current `since=` render gets a snapshot-clamp at execution.
- **r12-nit-4 — process risk: r9/r10 malfunctioned on context overflow since i058.** MOOT — the condense that
  produced THIS `.md`/`.md.full` split IS the ledger-split it asks for; at i062 all four affected lenses
  (r4/r6/r9/r10) re-ran FRESH on the `.md` and approved 0/0. the precondition it names is met.

> net i062: the two genuine L3 blockers (a real convergence bug + a real dead-WARN inconsistency, both on the
> flagship worktree-crew critipath) are closed at source with ONE structural addition that reuses canonical
> atomic-claim vocabulary; the four r11 nitpicks folded or HELD-with-rationale; r12's four nitpicks are
> already-tracked deferrals, one moot. no new surface area, no scope creep.
